# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Component Sunset / Removal Playbook

How a component stops being part of the design system. This is a fragment, not
a standalone document role: paste it into whatever plays the `deprecations`
role here (see `DEPRECATIONS.md.template` §4, "How a row gets here") and fill in
the `<!-- DECIDE -->` markers below it.

**Paste it into the `promoting-components` role instead** (see
`PROMOTING-COMPONENTS.md.template` §5, "Deprecating instead of promoting") if this
project has no `deprecations` role — which is the usual case for a project that
promotes components *into* a shared layer owned elsewhere, and so has nothing of
its own to deprecate. A project that publishes components should have the ledger,
and this playbook belongs beside it.

This is promotion's inverse. Promotion asks whether something has earned a
place in the shared layer; this asks how something leaves it without stranding
whoever still depends on it. The two should be read together — a project whose
promotion bar is clear but whose removal process is undefined just accumulates
components nobody can prove are safe to delete.

