## 1. What triggers a sunset

<!-- DECIDE: the actual signal — superseded by a newer component, zero call
     sites for a defined period, a design-system decision that the pattern
     itself is no longer sanctioned. A component does not get removed just
     because someone finds it distasteful; name the bar the way
     `PROMOTING-COMPONENTS.md.template` §1 names the promotion bar. -->

## 2. What sunsetting requires

Sunsetting is not a file deletion. All of these, or it is not sunset:

- [ ] Every call site identified — the layer-boundary rule in
      `PROMOTING-COMPONENTS.md.template` §4 means this is a closed, searchable
      set, not a guess
- [ ] A replacement named, if one exists, or an explicit decision recorded
      that there is none
- [ ] Marked deprecated for the grace period this project has decided on
      (see §3), not removed immediately
- [ ] Removed from the design document and the contributing document's
      lookup table in the same change that removes the code
- [ ] Removal recorded in `{{doc:decisions}}`, so "why did this disappear"
      has an answer later

